-- title:
--   At least two branches through singular special-fibre points
-- statement:
--   Let $p$ be a prime and $M$ a nonzero natural number with $5 \le M$ and $p \nmid M$; let $L$ be a field of characteristic zero which is a cyclotomic extension of $\mathbb{Q}$ of type $\{p\}$, and $\zeta \in L$ a primitive $p$-th root of unity. Let $K$ be the intermediate field of $L \subseteq \mathrm{LaurentSeries}\,L$ obtained by adjoining to $L$ the image, under the coefficientwise map $\mathrm{coeffEmb}\,L$ induced by $\mathbb{Q} \to L$, of the field of $q$-expansions attached to $\Gamma_1(Mp)$ (so $K =$ [`ModularCurve.laurentBaseChange L (ModularCurve.x1FunctionField (M * p))`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L103)). Let $A$ be a discrete valuation domain with an algebra structure on $L$ making $L$ its fraction field, such that $p$ lies in the maximal ideal of $A$ and $\zeta$ is in the image of $A$, with $A$ acting on $K$ compatibly through $L$, and let $\varpi$ generate the maximal ideal of $A$. Let $j \in K$ be nonzero and equal, as a Laurent series, to $\mathrm{coeffEmb}\,L$ applied to the $q$-expansion $q^{-1}\cdot \mathrm{jNumQ}$ of the modular invariant. Let $X =$ [`AlgebraicCurve.TwoChartIntegralModel A K j`](def/AlgebraicCurve_TwoChartIntegralModel.html#L236) be the scheme obtained by glueing $\operatorname{Spec}$ of the $A$-subalgebra of $K$ generated by $j$ and $\operatorname{Spec}$ of the $A$-subalgebra generated by $j^{-1}$ along the middle chart, with its structure morphism to $\operatorname{Spec} A$. Let $z$ be a point of $X$ and let $\varpi_z$ be the germ at $z$ of the global section of $X$ obtained by pulling $\varpi$ back along the structure morphism; assume $\varpi_z$ lies in the maximal ideal of the stalk $\mathcal{O}_{X,z}$ and that $\mathcal{O}_{X,z}/(\varpi_z)$ is not a regular local ring. Then the set of minimal primes of the ideal $(\varpi_z) \subseteq \mathcal{O}_{X,z}$ is not a subsingleton, i.e. it contains at least two distinct elements.
--
--   This is the statement that at a point of the special fibre of the two-chart integral model of $X_1(Mp)$ over the ring of integers of $\mathbb{Q}(\zeta_p)$ localised at $p$ at which the fibre fails to be regular, at least two algebraic branches of the special fibre pass through the point. It feeds the local description of such points (existence of $u, v$ with $uv = \varpi_z$ and $\mathfrak{m}_z = (u,v)$) and, contrapositively, the statement that points with a single branch lie in the smooth locus of the structure morphism.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_XOneP_not_subsingleton_minimalPrimes_span_germ_of_not_isRegularLocalRing_fibre_twoChartIntegralModel_x1_mul.lean

